# Sinfonia No. 3 in D major, BWV 789 (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: cheerful and steady. Three ideas run together in invertible
# counterpoint: the subject (paired sixteenths stepping down in a
# sequence), a walking eighth-note bass, and a chain of tied
# suspensions. A steady pulse throughout.
#
# Tempo: quarter = 84. Timings for 25 bars: Andras Schiff (clavichord,
# ECM) 1:13, about 82; Glenn Gould 1:08, about 88; Angela Hewitt 1:05,
# about 92. 84 is at the relaxed end of that range.
#
# Structure (my reading of the Mutopia score):
#   1-5    subject top 1-2, answer mid 3.5-4 (A major); cadence in
#          A major at bar 5 (beat 3).
#   6-12   subject in the bass 6-7; top entry 10.5-11 heading to
#          B minor; cadence in B minor at bar 12.
#   12-19  cadence in F# minor at bar 14 (beat 3); entries in E minor
#          top 14.5, mid 15; dominant pedal D in the bass (bar 18);
#          resolves to G at bar 19.
#   19-25  bass entry in G 19-20; return to the tonic: mid 21.5-22,
#          top 23.5-25; final cadence bar 25.

tempo 84
rit 1.5 0.7               # last bar and a half into the held final chord

dyn 1 mf                  # bars 1-11: exposition, bright
dyn 12 mp                 # bars 12-17: after the B minor cadence, the minor keys
ramp 18 mf                # bar 18: build over the D pedal into G
dyn 21.5 f                # bars 21-25: the subject back in D major

lead 1-2 top              # subject in the top
lead 3.5-4 mid            # answer in the middle
lead 6-7 bottom           # subject in the bass
lead 10.5-11 top          # top entry toward B minor
lead 14.5-15 top          # top entry in E minor
lead 15-16 mid            # middle entry in E minor
lead 19-20 bottom         # bass entry in G after the pedal
lead 21.5-22 mid          # middle entry back in D
lead 23.5-25 top          # last entry, top, into the cadence
